## Path Aliases (Use Always)

```typescript
@/components/*   → ./src/layouts/components/*
@/shortcodes/*   → ./src/layouts/shortcodes/*
@/helpers/*      → ./src/layouts/helpers/*
@/partials/*     → ./src/layouts/partials/*
@/*              → ./src/*
```

**Always use path aliases instead of relative imports.**

## Component Development

### Use .astro for Static Components

```astro
---
import config from "@/config/config.json";
import ImageMod from "@/components/ImageMod.astro";
import { slugSelector } from "@/lib/utils/languageParser";
import { humanize, slugify } from "@/lib/utils/textConverter";

const { data, lang } = Astro.props;
const { blog_folder } = config.settings;
---

<div class="bg-body dark:bg-darkmode-body">
  <ImageMod src={image} alt={title} width={445} height={230} format="webp" />
  <h4 class="mb-3">
    <a href={slugSelector(`/${blog_folder}/${data.id}`, lang)}>{title}</a>
  </h4>
</div>
```

### Use React (.tsx) for Interactive Components

- Place in `layouts/helpers/` for complex interactive features (e.g., LanguageSwitcher)
- Place in `layouts/shortcodes/` for MDX embeddable components
- Use `client:load`, `client:idle`, or `client:visible` directives
- Pass `lang` prop when component needs language awareness

```typescript
// layouts/shortcodes/Button.tsx
import React from "react";

const Button = ({
  label,
  link,
  style,
  rel,
}: {
  label: string;
  link: string;
  style?: string;
  rel?: string;
}) => {
  return (
    <a
      href={link}
      target={link.startsWith("http") ? "_blank" : "_self"}
      rel={`noopener noreferrer ${rel ? (rel === "follow" ? "" : rel) : "nofollow"}`}
      className={`btn ${style === "outline" ? "btn-outline-primary" : "btn-primary"}`}
    >
      {label}
    </a>
  );
};

export default Button;
```

## Content Collections

All content collections are defined in `src/content.config.ts` using Zod schemas:

- Use `glob` loader pattern from `astro/loaders`
- Define strict Zod schemas for type safety
- Common fields: `title`, `description`, `meta_title`, `date`, `image`, `draft`
- Blog posts include: `author`, `categories`, `tags`

## Configuration-Driven Design

The project is highly configuration-driven through JSON files:

- **Never hardcode** site settings, colors, or fonts
- **Always read** from `@/config/config.json` for site settings
- **Theme changes** go in `theme.json` (auto-generates `generated-theme.css`)
- **Language config** in `language.json` defines supported languages and content directories
- **Menu files** are language-specific: `menu.en.json`, `menu.fr.json`
- **Translation files** in `src/i18n/` contain UI text for each language
- Run `npm run generate-json` after config changes if needed

### Multilingual Settings in config.json

```json
{
  "settings": {
    "default_language": "en",
    "disable_languages": [],
    "default_language_in_subdir": false
  }
}
```

- `default_language`: Primary language code (e.g., "en")
- `disable_languages`: Array of language codes to disable (e.g., ["es"])
- `default_language_in_subdir`: If false, default language uses root URLs; if true, uses `/en/` prefix

