## Utility Functions (Always Use)

Located in `@/lib/utils/textConverter`:

- `slugify(content)` - Convert to URL-safe slug
- `humanize(content)` - Convert slug/underscore to readable text
- `markdownify(content, div?)` - Parse markdown to HTML
- `plainify(content)` - Strip HTML and markdown
- `dateFormat(date)` - Format dates consistently

Located in `@/lib/utils/languageParser`:

- `supportedLang` - Array of enabled language codes (includes empty string for default)
- `getLangFromUrl(url)` - Extract language from URL
- `getTranslations(lang)` - Get menu + dictionary for language
- `slugSelector(url, lang)` - Generate language-aware URLs

## Routing Conventions (Multilingual)

All pages are under `src/pages/[...lang]/` for multilingual support:

- `[...lang]` parameter captures language code or empty string for default language
- Routes: `/`, `/en/`, `/fr/` all supported
- Dynamic routes: `[single].astro`, `[slug].astro`
- Pagination: `page/[slug].astro` pattern
- Regular pages: `[regular].astro` for catch-all MD content

Example URL structure:
- Default language (`default_language_in_subdir: false`): `/blog`, `/about`
- English: `/en/blog`, `/en/about`
- French: `/fr/blog`, `/fr/about`

```astro
---
// src/pages/[...lang]/blog/index.astro
import { supportedLang } from "@/lib/utils/languageParser";

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return supportedLang.map((lang) => ({
    params: { lang: lang || undefined },
  }));
}

const { lang } = Astro.params;
const langCollection = lang as keyof ContentEntryMap;
const posts = await getSinglePage("blog", langCollection);
---
```

